{"data": [{"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113382874422386688"]}, "author_id": "215895007", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:31:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113382877358399739"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 9, "id": "5889072", "start": 0, "username": "wccftech"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/wccftech/statu…", "end": 278, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/wccftech/status/2113376629011669038", "start": 255, "url": "https://t.co/7pJtcJXcnd"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/x8gwKk6joY", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/juzzzzzzzzzzy/status/2113382877358399739/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113382874422386688", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/x8gwKk6joY"}]}, "id": "2113382877358399739", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113376629011669038", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "@wccftech Your next laptop is stuck in line behind a datacenter. Every wafer that becomes HBM for an AI cluster eats ~3x the silicon a PC stick would've used. Memory isn't expensive because PCs are hot, it's expensive because hyperscalers ate the supply. https://t.co/7pJtcJXcnd https://t.co/x8gwKk6joY", "url": "https://x.com/juzzzzzzzzzzy/status/2113382877358399739"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113375390265696256"]}, "author_id": "1010938256144420864", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:02:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113375392035639592"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/JMTpIShLNp", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/TechThought_org/status/2113375392035639592/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113375390265696256", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/JMTpIShLNp"}]}, "id": "2113375392035639592", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 8, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Researchers engineered perforated silicon modulators using slow light 💡 to boost optical signal conversion efficiency across datacenter networks.   \n\nReplacing power-hungry copper connections with ultra-compact optical links 🔌 drastically cuts thermal load and cluster latency. https://t.co/JMTpIShLNp", "url": "https://x.com/TechThought_org/status/2113375392035639592"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113331886760099840"]}, "author_id": "2112444660782452736", "created_at": "2026-10-22T23:00:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113405040048455845"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 243, "start": 235, "tag": "RSYSTEM"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/Rf3tsW9vDa", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/racksystemapp/status/2113405040048455845/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113331886760099840", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/Rf3tsW9vDa"}]}, "id": "2113405040048455845", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 117, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A project becomes more interesting when there’s something tangible behind the narrative.\n\nRACK has a defined GPU cluster, published technical specifications, and multiple compute plans for different workloads.\n\nFor anyone looking into $RSYSTEM, those are concrete starting points https://t.co/Rf3tsW9vDa", "url": "https://x.com/racksystemapp/status/2113405040048455845"}, {"author_id": "361572939", "created_at": "2026-10-22T23:19:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113409903167488270"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/evanjconrad/st…", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/evanjconrad/status/2113398162304163906", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/rTyEBvy2Vr"}]}, "id": "2113409903167488270", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 239, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113398162304163906", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "It’s obvious we are running into the physical limitations of power. No matter how many parallel datacenters you build or retrofit, power will be the stumbling block.\n\nDemand for compute will not go down. Supply will continue to be out paced and prices will increase in the short https://t.co/rTyEBvy2Vr", "url": "https://x.com/Gen_Page/status/2113409903167488270"}, {"author_id": "1856667903967330304", "created_at": "2026-10-22T23:02:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113405638092939448"], "id": "2113405638092939448", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "**Semiconductor lithography advances are resetting the global timeline for AI compute supremacy.**\n\n👇 Get the uncompromised strategy. ⤵️ Follow, Reply &amp; 💗 !\n\nEngineers have quietly breached sub-two-nanometer limits, threatening to invalidate existing geopolitical trade", "url": "https://x.com/WORLDINSIGHTCH/status/2113405638092939448"}, {"author_id": "5654932", "created_at": "2026-10-22T23:15:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113408855979831541"], "id": "2113408855979831541", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 221, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "HPE is expanding HPE Private Cloud AI with mixed-GPU clusters, larger configurations, and new interfaces for governed access to enterprise AI services. The update allows NVIDIA H200 and NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Server Edition GPUs to operate within a single cluster, giving", "url": "https://x.com/rtehrani/status/2113408855979831541"}, {"author_id": "1973441574186131462", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:17:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113379353790681588"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "AWS has added Training Sessions to SageMaker, giving developers more control over model-training steps while AWS manages the GPU work. The service is aimed at teams building models that need to learn from sequences of actions, such as agents that use tools. Its distinction is not that SageMaker can now fine-tune models or run reinforcement learning; both were already available. It is that teams can shape more of the training loop without configuring the underlying GPU infrastructure.", "display_url": "dataist.ai/news/aws-adds-…", "end": 227, "expanded_url": "https://dataist.ai/news/aws-adds-sagemaker-training-control-without-gpu-management/", "images": [{"height": 1024, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113379359130095616/FOmtBKLK?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1536}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113379359130095616/FOmtBKLK?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 204, "status": 200, "title": "AWS adds SageMaker training control without GPU management", "unwound_url": "https://dataist.ai/news/aws-adds-sagemaker-training-control-without-gpu-management/", "url": "https://t.co/sNEYzLEv0I"}]}, "id": "2113379353790681588", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AWS adds SageMaker training control without GPU management\n\nTraining Sessions lets SageMaker teams shape more of the training loop, but AWS offers no customer data on accuracy, cost or deployment speed.\n\nhttps://t.co/sNEYzLEv0I", "url": "https://x.com/neuronium_ai/status/2113379353790681588"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2113385066978017281"]}, "author_id": "767911033", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:42:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113385470101221670"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/KMuv6jJitu", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Andreyzila/status/2113385470101221670/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2113385066978017281", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/KMuv6jJitu"}]}, "id": "2113385470101221670", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "flapping airplanes raised $1b nine months after a $180m seed that valued it at $1.5b, reportedly $6b now. the  product is a megakernel: training, inference and vg in a single gpu kernel, overlapping memory bound inference with compute bound training so the chip rarely sits idle https://t.co/KMuv6jJitu", "url": "https://x.com/Andreyzila/status/2113385470101221670"}, {"author_id": "494126672", "created_at": "2026-10-22T23:02:57.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113405777066983608"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/i/status/21133…", "end": 195, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/i/status/2113383878215827664", "start": 172, "url": "https://t.co/mQpC3ICOFg"}]}, "id": "2113405777066983608", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 73, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113383878215827664", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "modal open-sourced the training server itself. your existing script runs unchanged, and you pay for gpu hours instead of per token. an api losing to a github link, love it https://t.co/mQpC3ICOFg", "url": "https://x.com/TSC/status/2113405777066983608"}, {"author_id": "1346351802111803393", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:58:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113389554095038560"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 28, "id": "117233133", "start": 19, "username": "cHHillee"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/modal/status/2…", "end": 242, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/modal/status/2113383878215827664", "start": 219, "url": "https://t.co/tyGwnw9cVA"}]}, "id": "2113389554095038560", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 12, "impression_count": 1585, "like_count": 27, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2113383878215827664", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I've been a fan of @cHHillee ever since \"Making Deep Learning Go Brrrr From First Principles\". If you had the tools to maximize GPU efficiency, could you own your post-training destiny? \n\nAlso hi this is my first tweet https://t.co/tyGwnw9cVA", "url": "https://x.com/micahisyong/status/2113389554095038560"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2113382478618501120"]}, "author_id": "1551987185372512263", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:35:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113383878215827664"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/I04rPmM2Yq", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/modal/status/2113383878215827664/video/1", "media_key": "13_2113382478618501120", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/I04rPmM2Yq"}]}, "id": "2113383878215827664", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 344, "impression_count": 61759, "like_count": 571, "quote_count": 22, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 35}, "text": "Tinker changed how people do post-training. We're big fans, and so are many of the teams we work with. But as those teams scale up, they keep raising the same two problems: per-token pricing gets expensive quickly, and you’re limited to the models and features the provider https://t.co/I04rPmM2Yq", "url": "https://x.com/modal/status/2113383878215827664"}, {"author_id": "1928480883717410816", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:03:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113375707321491485"], "id": "2113375707321491485", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A 30k-step training run cost us $0.26 of GPU time. Compute was never the expensive part; the feedback loop was. So we shipped a snapshot gate: evals now deploy and invoke mid-run checkpoints instead of waiting for the finish line. Tighten the loop, compound the work.", "url": "https://x.com/VargasJRDev/status/2113375707321491485"}, {"author_id": "1551376741402349568", "created_at": "2026-10-22T21:13:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113378301305893272"], "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 233, "start": 229, "tag": "ATH"}], "hashtags": [{"end": 238, "start": 234, "tag": "ATH"}, {"end": 249, "start": 239, "tag": "Inference"}, {"end": 253, "start": 250, "tag": "AI"}], "mentions": [{"end": 30, "id": "1531588175000268800", "start": 18, "username": "AethirCloud"}], "urls": [{"description": "Discover how AI inference spending surpassed training workloads in 2026 and why Aethir’s distributed GPU infrastructure is a great fit for inference workloads.", "display_url": "aethir.com/blog-posts/ai-…", "end": 278, "expanded_url": "https://aethir.com/blog-posts/ai-inference-spending-passed-training-the-55-shift", "images": [{"height": 900, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112668811631771649/wjUYYQ1e?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1600}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112668811631771649/wjUYYQ1e?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 255, "status": 200, "title": "AI Inference Spending Passed Training: The 55% Shift | Aethir", "unwound_url": "https://aethir.com/blog-posts/ai-inference-spending-passed-training-the-55-shift", "url": "https://t.co/vsjMSmzx0d"}]}, "id": "2113378301305893272", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 172, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "1/2🧵👇🏻\n🧠 Oct. 13: @AethirCloud says AI inference now accounts for 55% of AI-optimized IaaS spend in 2026—$23.3B vs $19B for training. Aethir argues distributed GPU supply fits inference better as demand shifts to serving models. $ATH #ATH #Inference #AI! https://t.co/vsjMSmzx0d", "url": "https://x.com/TimeIsMoneyHQ/status/2113378301305893272"}, {"author_id": "1859338255780446208", "created_at": "2026-10-22T23:04:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113406127174222272"], "id": "2113406127174222272", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "modal just open sourced spindle, a tinker compatible training server you run in your own modal workspace. your tinker scripts run unchanged and you pay for gpu time instead of per token\n\nalways fun when an api gets popular enough that someone ships a second implementation. kinda", "url": "https://x.com/RaghavMehtaM1/status/2113406127174222272"}, {"author_id": "1613862386829766656", "created_at": "2026-10-22T22:13:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113393223829729409"], "id": "2113393223829729409", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 208, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "KDDI company release, Oct 22: Broadcom is in the lab with them on co-packaged optics for AI data-center GPU fabrics.\n\nKDDI is standing up a test bed in its own AI data center and dropping in a CPO switch built around Broadcom Tomahawk 6 plus Davisson optical engines. Broadcom", "url": "https://x.com/AIInvestHK/status/2113393223829729409"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2112384777194233856"]}, "author_id": "2059876178119548928", "created_at": "2026-10-22T23:30:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113412586977005890"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/UXOo8oup7g", "end": 301, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/MaincodeAU/status/2113412586977005890/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2112384777194233856", "start": 278, "url": "https://t.co/UXOo8oup7g"}]}, "id": "2113412586977005890", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 138, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Why should you train your model with Matilda Train? \n\nMatilda train allows you to fine-tune your model and own everything that is produced, unlike other providers who will keep your model and charge you to serve it.\n\nYou will train on software that is 2.7x faster than the best https://t.co/UXOo8oup7g", "url": "https://x.com/MaincodeAU/status/2113412586977005890"}, {"author_id": "1536693901230321666", "created_at": "2026-10-22T22:45:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113401261286453369"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Bittensor is an open, decentralized network where independent subnets produce digital commodities — compute, inference, storage, prediction — and the chain pays contributors in TAO.", "display_url": "bittensor.com", "end": 104, "expanded_url": "https://bittensor.com", "images": [{"height": 675, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113401267045163008/RcTG_y1I?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113401267045163008/RcTG_y1I?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 81, "status": 200, "title": "Bittensor", "unwound_url": "https://www.bittensor.com/", "url": "https://t.co/SlwfCxp5uO"}, {"description": "Virtuals Protocol is a society of productive AI agents, each designed to generate services or products and autonomously engage in onchain commerce, with humans or other agents. These agents are tokenized through Agent Tokens, enabling capital formation, permissionless participation, and incentive alignment between creators, investors, and agents.", "display_url": "virtuals.io", "end": 218, "expanded_url": "https://virtuals.io", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112569712227782656/mR_PhPfb?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112569712227782656/mR_PhPfb?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 195, "status": 200, "title": "Virtuals Protocol | Society of AI Agents", "unwound_url": "https://www.virtuals.io/", "url": "https://t.co/l1mMOtKvyM"}]}, "id": "2113401261286453369", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 125, "impression_count": 52416, "like_count": 85, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "10 AI x CRYPTO PROJECTS / TOOLS WORTH KNOWING (BOOKMARK THIS):\n\n1. Bittensor\n    https://t.co/SlwfCxp5uO\n    → decentralized network where AI models compete and earn TAO\n2. Virtuals Protocol\n    https://t.co/l1mMOtKvyM\n    → platform for launching tokenized AI agents\n3.", "url": "https://x.co